From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:01:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: IR flash discovery LEDs

SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: IR flash discovery LEDs

Enable the PM8550 flash LED controller on the 13.8 inch Surface Laptop 7
with four IR LED nodes, one per flash channel, because the channel
Windows uses for the IR illuminator is unknown. Test only, to be replaced
by a single node once the channel is found (EMITTER-PLAN.md, stage B).

Each node is limited to the binding minimums: led-max-microamp 5000
(torch clamp), flash-max-microamp 12500 (12.5 mA, 1.8 % of Windows'
700 mA) and flash-max-timeout-us 10000 (10 ms PMIC safety timer), with
color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR> so the SL7 safety lockout in leds-qcom-flash
applies. They appear as ir:flash-1 to ir:flash-4. No camera node refers
to them: no st,leds, no leds = <...>, no led-names.

The nodes are in the DTB of every boot entry, but cannot bind outside the
IR test entry: leds-qcom-flash is loaded only by a modprobe gate that needs
sl7.ir_test=1 on the kernel command line, and the driver itself refuses IR
LED nodes unless ir_test=1.

Rationale: IR emitter bring-up, stage A.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -84,10 +84,12 @@
 	/*
 	 * IR camera, ST VD55G0 (ACPI CAMI, SMO55F0 / MSHW0472). Probe and
 	 * stream only: the illuminator is not connected. There is no `st,leds`
-	 * (the driver then keeps every sensor GPIO off) and no flash LED node.
+	 * (the driver then keeps every sensor GPIO off) and no `leds = <...>`
+	 * link to a flash LED.
 	 *
 	 * The illuminator is the PM8550 flash (QCOM0C27, 700 mA) but its
-	 * channel is unknown. Do not enable &pm8550_flash and do not add a
+	 * channel is unknown. The four discovery LEDs under &pm8550_flash
+	 * below are test-only and bind to nothing from this node. Do not add a
 	 * `leds = <...>` link until the channel has been found on the device
 	 * (see the Phase B notes). Never drive it as a continuous torch.
 	 *
@@ -158,6 +160,64 @@
  * HID over SPI in QSPI mode on QUP1 SE2. Wiring from the ACPI GTCH device:
  * SpiSerialBusV2 40 MHz mode 0, IRQ GPIO51, reset GPIO48, VDD enable GPIO64.
  */
+/*
+ * IR illuminator DISCOVERY ONLY (SL7 local, IR emitter plan stage A/B).
+ *
+ * One LED per PM8550 flash channel, because Windows' channel is unknown. Each
+ * is limited to the binding minimums: 12.5 mA flash, a 10 ms hardware safety
+ * timer, and a 5 mA torch clamp (torch itself is refused in code for any LED
+ * with color = IR). Replace these four nodes by one after Stage B.
+ *
+ * The node is in the DTB of every boot entry, but it can not bind outside the
+ * IR test entry: leds-qcom-flash is not loaded (modprobe gate: needs
+ * sl7.ir_test=1 on the kernel command line) and, if it were loaded anyway,
+ * its probe refuses IR LED nodes unless its module parameter ir_test=1
+ * (set only by that gate). No camera node refers to these LEDs.
+ */
+&pm8550_flash {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	led-0 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
+		function-enumerator = <1>;
+		led-sources = <1>;
+		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
+	};
+
+	led-1 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
+		function-enumerator = <2>;
+		led-sources = <2>;
+		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
+	};
+
+	led-2 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
+		function-enumerator = <3>;
+		led-sources = <3>;
+		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
+	};
+
+	led-3 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
+		function-enumerator = <4>;
+		led-sources = <4>;
+		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &spi10 {
 	compatible = "qcom,geni-spi-qspi";
 
